WEBVTT

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:16.500
In the midst of the noise,
he took a hard look at himself.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.450
Gymnast, Jotaro Aragaki...

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.950
People called him "Samurai."

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:31.450
In 1992, when he graduated high school,
he joined a corporate team

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.250
and won a bronze medal at his first Olympics.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:40.700
Four years later, in August of this year,
at his second Olympics,

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:46.410
he won a silver medal and caused
a wave of samurai fever across Japan.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.330
On his days off, he spends time with his family.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:53.580
He married the popular actress, Tomoyo Mifune,

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.620
and they have one daughter.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:01.950
I just want to show my wife
and daughter my gymnastics.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.200
"Gymnast Aragaki retires not!?"

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.790
"Gymnast Aragaki retires not!?"

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.790
Right, so that was a documentary
from six years ago.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.120
"Gymnast Aragaki retires not!?"

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.120
Anyway, he has had a
wonderful career as a gymnast.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.080
"Gymnast Aragaki retires not!?"

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.080
There has always been
something odd about him, though.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.500
"Gymnast Aragaki retires not!?"

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.500
But that's what's cute about him!

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:24.580
I also love Mr. Aragaki, and personally,
I was hoping for a more samurai-like end.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.580
I wonder what his coach,
Amakusa thought about it.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.660
You stupid idiot!

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.700
With this press conference,

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.450
there have been voices saying
he's pulling a "fake retirement" or "fake--

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.040
"Gymnast Aragaki was
to announce retirement, but..."
...retire not.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.580
"At gymnast Aragaki's
retirement press conference..."
...will retire...

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:44.790
...not.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.000
Not?

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.410
Meanwhile, there is also encouraging news
from the gymnastics world.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:55.250
Yes, the high school student no one in the
gymnastics world can take their eyes off of--

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.580
--the "Bandana Prince," Tetsuo Minamino!
--Hm?

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.700
"Savior of gymnastics! 'Bandana Prince'"

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.700
Achieving top scores at All-Japan the other day,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.910
"Savior of gymnastics! 'Bandana Prince'"

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.910
he's also been called the savior
of Japanese gymnastics.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.580
"Savior of gymnastics! 'Bandana Prince'"

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.580
We talked to him after practice.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.000
"Q. How do you feel about the current
state of Japanese gymnastics?"

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.580
"Q. How do you feel about the current
state of Japanese gymnastics?"

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.580
Nothing much.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.950
"Q. Do you think Japanese gymnastics
will get better in the future?"

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.870
"Q. Do you think Japanese gymnastics
will get better in the future?"

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.870
I just have to win.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:49.870
"The Gymnastics Samurai"

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.790
Oh, hello, Mr. Aragaki!

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.040
I'm from Pathos Weekly!

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.700
About yesterday's press conference--

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.870
Did you retract your retirement at the point

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.950
due to some kind of conflict with your coach?

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:02.790
No.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:05.410
Your scores have not been
very favorable recently.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:08.410
Does this mean you think you can still continue?

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.950
Yes, I think so...

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.870
Do you think you could give us
some more interesting remarks?

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.580
What are you people doing?!

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:23.200
I don't remember giving
permission for an interview.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.450
I'm sorry for what I did despite
all the preparations you made.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.160
I think I can still do it.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.330
Please let me try one more time.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:49.540
It's true that I might be less powerful now.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.330
But I'll make up for it by practicing
harder than I ever have before!

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.250
If I practice more than anyone--

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.700
That's enough.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.040
If you say you'll continue no matter what,
then do what you want.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.540
But I won't have anything to do with it.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.540
Amakusa!

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.200
There is no place for you at this club.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:21.290
Don't let me see your face again.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.330
"Episode 2 'Rock-Bottom Samurai'"

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:25.250
"Episode 2 'Rock-Bottom Samurai'"

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:25.250
Huh? What did you say?

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.410
"Episode 2 'Rock-Bottom Samurai'"

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.410
I was fired from the club...

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.120
Rachel, what's the matter?

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.450
Dad said he was fired...

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:39.910
Joe, you're a fugitive, too?!

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.250
You can't let that happen!

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.540
That's no good!

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.540
No good! No good!

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.410
That's no good!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.040
Bigbird, be quiet!

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:53.120
Anyway, you need to go apologize
to Mr. Amakusa again.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.830
He said he didn't want to see my face again...

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:56.250
Huh?

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:00.000
It was the first time
I'd ever seen him that angry.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.540
Don't worry.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.080
I'll get him to forgive me somehow.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.450
I have to think about what
I can do on my own until then.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.700
"Warm-up"
"Running" "Trampoline" "Stretch" "Core" "Rings"
"Parallettes and parallel bars" "Resistance band"

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:20.660
I said I'd think about it,
but I don't have any equipment...

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.790
What should I do with my training plan...?

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.450
"Running"
"Warm-up"

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.580
I guess I'll try this...

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.290
Thanks for the food, indeed.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:46.700
Rei, I'll wash the dishes today.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.290
--Ouch!
--Ow! Ow!

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.700
Are you okay, Dad?

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:57.450
C-C-C-C-Cramp... C-C-C...

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.790
Just how much did you run?

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:01.700
Six hours.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.120
That's too much!

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.500
I am ashamed.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.040
"Resistance band"

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.040
Dad...

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:25.160
Scared, bastard?

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.000
Hm?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.000
Think you can win against me,
a former Green Beret?

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.330
Wanna try me?

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.870
I've even defeated creatures
from another planet before.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.000
Oh, Joe!

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.370
Oh, stop, Leo!

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.540
We're pretending we're in a movie!

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:41.080
If you're free, why don't you join us?

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.160
I said, stop!

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:47.870
He's doing visualization practice,
so you can't bother him!

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.620
Sorry, Dad.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.410
I'll play with Leo, so don't worry about us.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.540
Pretending to be in a movie, huh?

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.660
Things look lively around here.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.700
Lady Mari! Look, look!

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:02.870
Did we wake you up, Grandma?

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.410
It's fine.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:07.620
More importantly, if you're planning
to keep freeloading here,

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.750
then why don't you at least find
a way to pay for living expenses?

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.200
Huh?

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.620
Come and try working at my place.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.450
It's called "work."

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:17.330
A mission, indeed?

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.700
That's right. Starting tonight.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:23.040
Tonight! I'll show you
the power of a ninja, indeed!

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.410
Then, you want me to go help, too--

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.870
You're no good at serving customers, remember?

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.580
I'm Ayu!

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.000
This is some bizarre fashion, indeed!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.750
<i>Баркалла.</i>

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:42.160
I-I am Leo, indeed. I am a ninja.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:44.000
I am pleased to meet you, indeed.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.950
Crazy. That's, like, totally hilarious.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:49.120
For now, just let him
try doing different things.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:50.410
'Kay!

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:56.700
There are people from many
different villages here, indeed.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.080
"Villages," lol.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.370
Here, it doesn't matter what
your job is or how old you are.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:03.330
We accept those who come

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:05.160
and do not chase those who leave.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:08.750
And we do <i>not </i>pry at all.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.580
I told you, I don't get that hard stuff.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.000
That's 'bukuro for you.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.040
Here!

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:18.580
Take these to Bri.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.660
Roger Dodger!

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.660
Thanks for waiting, indeed.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.080
Thanks.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.830
What are you doing?!

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.660
As expected, you have nice legs.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:34.040
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.120
I-I am a simple ninja, indeed.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.620
Oh? Really.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:42.200
If you're injured, let me know.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:46.080
I'll stick you with needles <i>anytime</i>.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.120
What're you saying?!

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.750
Without alcohol, your hands shake so much,
you'd stick 'em into unthinkable places!

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.120
Shut up, old man!

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:55.540
Remember what you did to me?

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:58.120
When you were tired, instead of using a needle,
you used a nail on my pressure point,

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.370
hitting it with a hammer
until blood spurted out.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.700
Idiot!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.450
I'm Britney.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.870
Here, take this.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:11.000
And make sure you <i>don't lose it</i>.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.540
"Standing back somersault"
"Straight back somersault"

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:25.830
I'll try it right away.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:29.580
Ouch!

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.250
Dad?!

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:37.290
Leo, make sure you don't
get in the way of Dad's training.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:38.620
Understood, indeed!

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.790
I'll buy a new light during my run.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:42.830
Good.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.290
Not a single thing is going well...

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:58.450
Ow! Watch where yer goin'...!

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:01.830
Get outta here!

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:03.040
This is <i>my </i>territory!

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.830
This is <i>my </i>park!

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.200
I <i>made </i>this place!

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.450
I'm the one who <i>told </i>you to!

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.500
Huh?

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.330
I'm home, indeed!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.330
Joe, I'm back!

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.950
Work was fun today, too!

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:34.120
And when I don't know
what to do, everyone helps me.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:40.580
Joe, what's the matter?

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:46.120
I was also

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:49.330
always getting help from others...

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:52.540
I want to make Rei smile with my gymnastics...

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:56.120
I thought I could make it
work somehow on my own,

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:58.250
but forget being a gymnast...

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:02.700
I was failing as a father...

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:06.790
Joe, what? What did you say?

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:10.410
There's no way I can ask
Amakusa to forgive me like this...

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:13.080
I've already got my shoulder injury...

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.250
It's only natural for him to give up on me.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.410
Injury?

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:18.790
Joe, are you injured?

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.830
Yeah...

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:25.410
If you're injured, then get it healed!

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.790
Roger Dodger!

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:31.790
"Kawamoto Orthopedic Clinic"

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:32.620
"Kawamoto Orthopedic Clinic"
"Acupuncture and Moxibustion​"

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.000
"Kawamoto Orthopedic Clinic"
"Acupuncture and Moxibustion​"

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.000
Is this the place?

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.250
--Come now, one and all,
it is time for the raid, indeed!

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:39.200
--Hey! W-Wait! Don't push me! I said, don't push!
--Come now, one and all,
it is time for the raid, indeed!

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.750
Is she dead?

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:51.580
Oh, she's alive! I'm glad!

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:57.870
U-Um, is it all right to go in...?

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:02.540
Seriously...?

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:03.910
Joe!

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:05.450
Over here! Over here!

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:16.950
Oh, my.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:18.450
Oh, my!

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:19.660
Oh, my...

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:22.750
You've got a bad shoulder, right?

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.370
H-How did you know?

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.080
Come, take off your clothes and lie down.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.120
Huh?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.200
--Huh?
--Yeah!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.620
Huh?

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.290
How did you know about my shoulder?

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.450
Hm?

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:39.290
I heard from Leo.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.250
Huh?

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.950
What, you called?

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:43.700
I'll do my best!

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:46.080
Because I want to see Joe's gymnastics!

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:50.250
Now, it's stabby-stab time.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.450
Okay, time to get up.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:06.160
Well? Are you healed?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.660
It feels different!

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.950
Who do you think treated you?

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:19.500
That was a close one.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:24.540
If you had started training seriously
in your current condition,

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:27.330
that shoulder would've exploded.

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:28.410
Boom!

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:30.370
"Boom"?!

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.700
I'm not trying to scare you,

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:35.750
but I <i>am </i>involved in medical treatment.

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:37.200
That's why I know...

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:41.290
It's a grave case that's
a matter of life and death.

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:45.290
My shoulder would explode, and I'd die?!

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:47.540
Here.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:53.120
For now, practice tai chi every morning.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:55.950
I'll teach you in great detail.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:59.830
Will tai chi prevent the explosion?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:02.500
Without causing stress to the body,

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.870
tai chi can build up physical strength,
core strength, and stamina.

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:07.830
Start with that first.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:10.500
That, and regular acupuncture.

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:14.660
Um, if I were to practice--

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:15.750
Forget about it!

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:19.000
You'll really die, damn it!

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.250
Right.

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:34.540
Is it really okay to be doing
something like this?

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.200
Stabby...

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.370
...and stab...

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.910
"Kawamoto Orthopedic Clinic"
"Acupuncture and Moxibustion​"

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.500
Well? How does your body feel?

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.660
It feels pretty good.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:28.540
Hey, have you ever heard
of overtraining syndrome?

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.040
No...

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:33.330
It's not that well-known in Japan yet.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:39.830
Simply put, it's when you train too much
and your body is constantly fatigued.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.620
Fatigued...

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:44.000
If it's allowed to continue
on its normal course,

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.790
you could even become depressed.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:48.080
It's a very scary condition...

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:51.540
You were on the verge of developing it.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:53.410
It didn't matter what it was,

00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:57.950
as long as you took a break from
gymnastics and let your body rest.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.790
Jotaro.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:06.330
I'm just... a little tired.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.450
I think you should give
your body a break after all.

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:10.870
It's turning into a vicious cycle.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:13.370
What'll you do if you work too hard
and hurt your shoulder again?

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:14.370
I can do it.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:17.870
I can't win if I don't make up for it
with how much I practice...!

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:21.370
Hey, listen to what I'm saying once in a while!

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:27.950
Is that the coach who told you to retire?

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:29.200
Yes.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:33.200
I see.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:55.330
Tomoyo... I'm an idiot...

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:02.040
What? I don't have much time.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:06.250
Amakusa! I am truly sorry!

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:10.450
I didn't see myself at all!

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:12.370
I trusted too much in my body and technique,

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:16.200
and even when I was feeling bad,
I thought I could definitely do it...

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:21.250
That's why I didn't understand how you felt
at all when you told me to retire...

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:26.200
But I finally... finally understand!

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:29.750
Will you be my coach again?

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:36.830
From now on, I'll listen
properly to what you say!

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:39.580
I'm completely hopeless by myself...

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:43.830
At this rate, I...

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:50.410
Please! Just one more chance!

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:53.000
Please give me one more
chance to fight with you!

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.540
Please!

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:09.660
A samurai shouldn't act like that.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:12.790
Listen, Jotaro.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:18.290
Considering your age, your stamina
and technique will only decline.

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:21.040
Your shoulder's a ticking time bomb, too.

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:26.660
Even if I give it my all,
I can't reverse that fact.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:34.370
All I can do is work with you to come up
with a way to fight against that.

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:41.290
It's a completely unknown world for me, too.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.790
Please.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:49.580
Jeez, learning from scratch again at this age...

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:55.540
Amakusa...

00:19:55.540 --> 00:20:00.160
Anyway, let's see how far we can get.

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:01.910
Thank you very much!

00:20:05.790 --> 00:20:10.160
What happened to you while you were gone?

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:13.200
My acupuncturist helped me realize.

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:14.620
Acupuncturist?

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:18.120
Yes. Leo introduced me.

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:19.660
I see...

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:22.950
Then you should be grateful to that ninja.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:26.250
I suppose...

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:28.500
"Yotsuba Sports"

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:29.750
"Yotsuba Sports"

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:29.750
Leo.

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:31.410
Time to go.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.450
Joe!

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:33.790
How did it go?

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.250
I'll start my comeback tomorrow.

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:38.700
--Really?
--Oh, Jotaro!

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:40.500
Tackey!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:42.700
Leomaru!

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:45.330
Hey! Yay!

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:49.370
Oh, Jotaro, what've you
been doing all this time?

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:51.870
Oh... I was fired...

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:56.000
No way, Amakusa was super scared, you know.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.830
He was like, "Have you heard from Jotaro?"

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:01.830
and "Have you heard about him
going to other clubs?"

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:04.410
He asked me like 5,000 times!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:19.370
I look forward to working
with you from now on, too.

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:20.540
Yeah!

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:32.250
Hm?

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:39.700
You are an embarrassment to gymnastics, damn it!

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:43.790
Huh?
